{"id":"mahabharata-1-053","work":"mahabharata","part":1,"partName":"आदिपर्व","partNameEn":"Adi Parva","unit":53,"title":"त्रिपञ्चाशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 53 · The sacrifice ends and the snakes bless Astika","summary":{"en":"Takshaka is held fast in the air by Astika's word, and the king grants the boon and ends the sacrifice, honouring Astika. The grateful snakes promise that whoever recites this story will be safe from them, and Shaunaka now asks to hear the Bharata itself.","kn":"ಆಸ್ತೀಕನ ಮಾತಿನಿಂದ ತಕ್ಷಕನು ಆಕಾಶದಲ್ಲೇ ನಿಲ್ಲುತ್ತಾನೆ; ರಾಜನು ವರ ನೀಡಿ ಯಜ್ಞ ನಿಲ್ಲಿಸಿ ಆಸ್ತೀಕನನ್ನು ಸನ್ಮಾನಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಈ ಕಥೆಯನ್ನು ಪಠಿಸುವವರಿಗೆ ತಮ್ಮಿಂದ ಭಯವಿಲ್ಲವೆಂದು ಕೃತಜ್ಞ ಸರ್ಪಗಳು ವಾಗ್ದಾನ ಮಾಡುತ್ತವೆ; ಶೌನಕರು ಈಗ ಭಾರತವನ್ನು ಕೇಳಬಯಸುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"आस्तीक के वचन से तक्षक आकाश में ही रुक जाता है; राजा वर देकर यज्ञ समाप्त करते हैं और आस्तीक का सम्मान करते हैं। कृतज्ञ सर्प वचन देते हैं कि इस कथा का पाठ करने वाले को उनसे भय नहीं होगा, और शौनक अब भारत-कथा सुनना चाहते हैं।","te":"ఆస్తీకుని మాటతో తక్షకుడు ఆకాశంలోనే నిలిచిపోతాడు; రాజు వరమిచ్చి యజ్ఞం ఆపి ఆస్తీకుని సత్కరిస్తాడు. ఈ కథను పఠించేవారికి తమ వల్ల భయం ఉండదని కృతజ్ఞతగల సర్పాలు వాగ్దానం చేస్తాయి; శౌనకుడు ఇప్పుడు భారతాన్ని వినగోరుతాడు.","ta":"ஆஸ்தீகரின் சொல்லால் தக்ஷகன் வானிலேயே நிற்கிறான்; மன்னன் வரமளித்து யாகத்தை நிறுத்தி ஆஸ்தீகரைக் கௌரவிக்கிறான். இக்கதையைப் படிப்பவர்களுக்குத் தம்மால் அச்சமில்லை என்று நன்றியுள்ள நாகங்கள் வாக்களிக்கின்றன; ஶௌனகர் இப்போது பாரதக் கதையைக் கேட்க விரும்புகிறார்.","ml":"ആസ്തികന്റെ വാക്കിനാൽ തക്ഷകൻ ആകാശത്ത് ഉറച്ചുനിൽക്കുന്നു; രാജാവ് വരം അനുവദിച്ച് യജ്ഞം അവസാനിപ്പിക്കുകയും ആസ്തികനെ ആദരിക്കുകയും ചെയ്യുന്നു. നന്ദിയുള്ള പാമ്പുകൾ, ഈ കഥ ചൊല്ലുന്നവർക്ക് തങ്ങളിൽനിന്ന് ഭയമില്ലെന്ന് വാഗ്ദാനം ചെയ്യുന്നു; ശൗനകൻ ഇനി ഭാരതം തന്നെ കേൾക്കാൻ ആവശ്യപ്പെടുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 1.53; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Thu Aug 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"आस्तीकपर्व","titleEn":"Astika Parva","verses":[{"text":"सूत उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Suta said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"इदमत्यद्भुतं चान्यदास्तीकस्यानुशुश्रुमः ।\nतथा वरैश्छन्द्यमाने राज्ञा पारिक्षितेन ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"We have heard another very wondrous thing about Astika, from the time when King Parikshit's son was being pressed to grant boons."}},{"n":2,"text":"इन्द्रहस्ताच्च्युतो नागः ख एव यदतिष्ठत ।\nततश्चिन्तापरो राजा बभूव जनमेजयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The serpent, slipped from Indra's hand, stayed right there in the sky; and King Janamejaya became anxious."}},{"n":3,"text":"हूयमाने भृशं दीप्ते विधिवत्पावके तदा ।\nन स्म स प्रापतद्वह्नौ तक्षको भयपीडितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Though the offerings were being poured intensely into the properly kindled fire, Takshaka, tormented with fear, did not fall into it."}},{"text":"शौनक उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Shaunaka said:"}},{"n":4,"text":"किं सूत तेषां विप्राणां मन्त्रग्रामो मनीषिणाम् ।\nन प्रत्यभात्तदाग्नौ यन्न पपात स तक्षकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Suta, why did the whole body of mantras of those wise brahmins fail to work, so that Takshaka did not fall into the fire?"}},{"text":"सूत उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Suta said:"}},{"n":5,"text":"तमिन्द्रहस्ताद्विस्रस्तं विसंज्ञं पन्नगोत्तमम् ।\nआस्तीकस्तिष्ठ तिष्ठेति वाचस्तिस्रोऽभ्युदैरयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the best of serpents slipped from Indra's hand, senseless, Astika spoke three times the words \"Stay, stay, stay.\""}},{"n":6,"text":"वितस्थे सोऽन्तरिक्षेऽथ हृदयेन विदूयता ।\nयथा तिष्ठेत वै कश्चिद्गोचक्रस्यान्तरा नरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then he hung in mid-air, his heart trembling, like a man standing in the middle of a cart wheel."}},{"n":7,"text":"ततो राजाब्रवीद्वाक्यं सदस्यैश्चोदितो भृशम् ।\nकाममेतद्भवत्वेवं यथास्तीकस्य भाषितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the king, strongly urged by the assembly, said: \"Let it be so, as Astika has said.\""}},{"n":8,"text":"समाप्यतामिदं कर्म पन्नगाः सन्त्वनामयाः ।\nप्रीयतामयमास्तीकः सत्यं सूतवचोऽस्तु तत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Let this rite be completed; let the serpents be unharmed; let Astika be pleased; let Suta's word come true.\""}},{"n":9,"text":"ततो हलहलाशब्दः प्रीतिजः समवर्तत ।\nआस्तीकस्य वरे दत्ते तथैवोपरराम च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then a joyful roar arose; when Astika's boon was granted, the sacrifice also stopped."}},{"n":10,"text":"स यज्ञः पाण्डवेयस्य राज्ञः पारिक्षितस्य ह ।\nप्रीतिमांश्चाभवद्राजा भारतो जनमेजयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That sacrifice of the Pandava king, Parikshit's son, ended, and King Janamejaya of Bharata's line was pleased."}},{"n":11,"text":"ऋत्विग्भ्यः ससदस्येभ्यो ये तत्रासन्समागताः ।\nतेभ्यश्च प्रददौ वित्तं शतशोऽथ सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"To the priests and assembly members and all who had gathered there, the king gave wealth by the hundreds and thousands."}},{"n":12,"text":"लोहिताक्षाय सूताय तथा स्थपतये विभुः ।\nयेनोक्तं तत्र सत्राग्रे यज्ञस्य विनिवर्तनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The lord also gave much wealth to Suta Lohitaksha and the builder, who had said at the start of the sacrifice that a brahmin would be the reason it would end."}},{"n":13,"text":"निमित्तं ब्राह्मण इति तस्मै वित्तं ददौ बहु ।\nततश्चकारावभृथं विधिदृष्टेन कर्मणा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then he performed the concluding bath by the rite shown in the rules."}},{"n":14,"text":"आस्तीकं प्रेषयामास गृहानेव सुसत्कृतम् ।\nराजा प्रीतमनाः प्रीतं कृतकृत्यं मनीषिणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king, pleased in mind, sent Astika home with great honor, a satisfied, wise man who had accomplished his purpose."}},{"n":15,"text":"पुनरागमनं कार्यमिति चैनं वचोऽब्रवीत् ।\nभविष्यसि सदस्यो मे वाजिमेधे महाक्रतौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"He said to him: \"You must come again; you will be a member of my assembly at the great horse sacrifice.\""}},{"n":16,"text":"तथेत्युक्त्वा प्रदुद्राव स चास्तीको मुदा युतः ।\nकृत्वा स्वकार्यमतुलं तोषयित्वा च पार्थिवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Saying \"So be it,\" Astika went off joyfully, having done his incomparable task and pleased the king."}},{"n":17,"text":"स गत्वा परमप्रीतो मातरं मातुलं च तम् ।\nअभिगम्योपसंगृह्य यथावृत्तं न्यवेदयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Very glad, he went to his mother and his uncle, and approached them, embraced their feet, and told them all as it had happened."}},{"n":18,"text":"एतच्छ्रुत्वा प्रीयमाणाः समेता\nये तत्रासन्पन्नगा वीतमोहाः ।\nतेऽऽस्तीके वै प्रीतिमन्तो बभूवु-\nरूचुश्चैनं वरमिष्टं वृणीष्व ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing this, the serpents gathered there, pleased and freed of their confusion, became fond of Astika and said to him: \"Choose the boon you desire.\""}},{"n":19,"text":"भूयो भूयः सर्वशस्तेऽब्रुवंस्तं\nकिं ते प्रियं करवामोऽद्य विद्वन् ।\nप्रीता वयं मोक्षिताश्चैव सर्वे\nकामं किं ते करवामोऽद्य वत्स ॥","meaning":{"en":"Again and again they all said to him: \"Learned one, what can we do today that you would like? We are pleased, and all of us are freed. What wish of yours can we fulfill today, child?\""}},{"text":"आस्तीक उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Astika said:"}},{"n":20,"text":"सायं प्रातः सुप्रसन्नात्मरूपा\nलोके विप्रा मानवाश्चेतरेऽपि ।\nधर्माख्यानं ये वदेयुर्ममेदं\nतेषां युष्मद्भ्यो नैव किंचिद्भयं स्यात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Let brahmins and other people in the world, evening and morning, in good cheer, who tell this account of dharma of mine, have no fear whatever from you.\""}},{"text":"सूत उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Suta said:"}},{"n":21,"text":"तैश्चाप्युक्तो भागिनेयः प्रसन्नै-\nरेतत्सत्यं काममेवं चरन्तः ।\nप्रीत्या युक्ता ईप्सितं सर्वशस्ते\nकर्तारः स्म प्रवणा भागिनेय ॥","meaning":{"en":"And the pleased serpents said to their sister's son: \"This is true; we will do what you wish. Joined in affection, we will happily do your desire in everything, nephew.\""}},{"n":22,"text":"जरत्कारोर्जरत्कार्वां समुत्पन्नो महायशाः ।\nआस्तीकः सत्यसंधो मां पन्नगेभ्योऽभिरक्षतु ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Let Astika, the renowned son of Jaratkaru by Jaratkaru, true to his promise, protect me from the serpents.\""}},{"n":23,"text":"असितं चार्तिमन्तं च सुनीथं चापि यः स्मरेत् ।\nदिवा वा यदि वा रात्रौ नास्य सर्पभयं भवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Whoever remembers Asita, Artiman and Sunitha, by day or by night, will have no fear of snakes.\""}},{"text":"सूत उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Suta said:"}},{"n":24,"text":"मोक्षयित्वा स भुजगान्सर्पसत्राद्द्विजोत्तमः ।\nजगाम काले धर्मात्मा दिष्टान्तं पुत्रपौत्रवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having freed the serpents from the snake sacrifice, that best of brahmins, righteous in soul, in time met his end, with sons and grandsons."}},{"n":25,"text":"इत्याख्यानं मयास्तीकं यथावत्कीर्तितं तव ।\nयत्कीर्तयित्वा सर्पेभ्यो न भयं विद्यते क्वचित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So I have told you the story of Astika as it happened; by reciting it, there is no fear of serpents anywhere."}},{"n":26,"text":"श्रुत्वा धर्मिष्ठमाख्यानमास्तीकं पुण्यवर्धनम् ।\nआस्तीकस्य कवेर्विप्र श्रीमच्चरितमादितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having heard, brahmin, this most righteous story of Astika, which increases merit, the splendid history of the wise Astika from the beginning, (Shaunaka replied as follows)."}},{"text":"शौनक उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Shaunaka said:"}},{"n":27,"text":"भृगुवंशात्प्रभृत्येव त्वया मे कथितं महत् ।\nआख्यानमखिलं तात सौते प्रीतोऽस्मि तेन ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"You have told me the great story in full, starting from the line of Bhrigu, son of Suta, and I am pleased with you for it."}},{"n":28,"text":"प्रक्ष्यामि चैव भूयस्त्वां यथावत्सूतनन्दन ।\nयां कथां व्याससंपन्नां तां च भूयः प्रचक्ष्व मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"And I will ask you more, son of Suta; tell me again that tale which Vyasa composed."}},{"n":29,"text":"तस्मिन्परमदुष्प्रापे सर्पसत्रे महात्मनाम् ।\nकर्मान्तरेषु विधिवत्सदस्यानां महाकवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"At that very hard-to-obtain snake sacrifice, in the pauses between the rites, great poet, what varied stories did the great-souled assembly members tell, on what subjects?"}},{"n":30,"text":"या बभूवुः कथाश्चित्रा येष्वर्थेषु यथातथम् ।\nत्वत्त इच्छामहे श्रोतुं सौते त्वं वै विचक्षणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"We wish to hear them from you, Sauti, for you are skilled."}},{"text":"सूत उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Suta said:"}},{"n":31,"text":"कर्मान्तरेष्वकथयन्द्विजा वेदाश्रयाः कथाः ।\nव्यासस्त्वकथयन्नित्यमाख्यानं भारतं महत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the pauses of the rites, the brahmins told tales based on the Veda; but Vyasa recited constantly the great story of the Bharatas."}},{"text":"शौनक उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Shaunaka said:"}},{"n":32,"text":"महाभारतमाख्यानं पाण्डवानां यशस्करम् ।\nजनमेजयेन यत्पृष्टः कृष्णद्वैपायनस्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great story of the Mahabharata, which brings renown to the Pandavas, was what Krishna Dvaipayana, when asked by Janamejaya,"}},{"n":33,"text":"श्रावयामास विधिवत्तदा कर्मान्तरेषु सः ।\nतामहं विधिवत्पुण्यां श्रोतुमिच्छामि वै कथाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"then recited in due manner in the pauses of the rites. I wish to hear that sacred tale properly,"}},{"n":34,"text":"मनःसागरसंभूतां महर्षेः पुण्यकर्मणः ।\nकथयस्व सतां श्रेष्ठ न हि तृप्यामि सूतज ॥","meaning":{"en":"born from the ocean of the mind of the great sage of holy deeds. Tell it, best of good men; I am not yet satisfied, son of Suta."}},{"text":"सूत उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Suta said:"}},{"n":35,"text":"हन्त ते कथयिष्यामि महदाख्यानमुत्तमम् ।\nकृष्णद्वैपायनमतं महाभारतमादितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Gladly I will tell you the great and excellent story, the Mahabharata as Krishna Dvaipayana conceived it, from the beginning."}},{"n":36,"text":"तज्जुषस्वोत्तममते कथ्यमानं मया द्विज ।\nशंसितुं तन्मनोहर्षो ममापीह प्रवर्तते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Listen to it as I tell it, brahmin of excellent mind; the joy of my heart also stirs to tell it."}}]}]}